/**
 * @page dev_stream_config SDR device stream configuration
 * 
 * @section creating_stream Creating stream
 * 
 * Once the SDR device parameter configuration is finished, a stream object must be created to begin streaming data. Stream is created via previously created device interface by invoking
 * @ref lime::SDRDevice::StreamCreate(const lime::StreamConfig&, uint8_t) "StreamCreate()" function. The stream parameters (packet size, PPS and etc.) must be set up beforehand using
 * @ref lime::StreamConfig "StreamConfig" structure. Example of stream creation:
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <iostream>
 * #include <vector>
 * #include <memory>
 * #include <limesuiteng/DeviceRegistry.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/SDRDevice.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/RFStream.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/StreamConfig.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/DeviceHandle.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/SDRConfig.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/ToString.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/OpStatus.h>
 * 
 * int main()
 * {
 *    ... // SDR device discovery, registration and configuration
 * 
 *    uint8_t moduleIndex = 0;   // For SDR device with single RF chip
 *    
 *    // Setting up stream configuration
 *    lime::StreamConfig miniStreamConf = {};   // Stream configuration with default values
 *    std::unique_ptr<lime::RFStream> miniStream = device->StreamCreate(miniStreamConf, moduleIndex);
 * 
 *    ... // Other program code   
 *       
 *    lime::DeviceRegistry::freeDevice(device); // End of program code
 *    return 0;
 * }
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @subsection stream_parameters Stream parameters
 * 
 * Here is a detailed list of @ref lime::StreamConfig "StreamConfig" structure members with additional information about each parameter below the table:
 * <table>
 *    <tr>
 *       <th> Parameter </th>
 *       <th> Units/Options </th>
 *       <th> Default initialized value </th>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Packet size </td>
 *       <td> Sample count </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Batch size </td>
 *       <td> Packet count </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Format </td>
 *       <td> I12 or I16 </td>
 *       <td> I16 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Link format </td>
 *       <td> I12 or I16 </td>
 *       <td> I16 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Data buffer size </td>
 *       <td> Bytes </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Channel </td>
 *       <td> Tx [0 1] and Rx [0 1] </td>
 *       <td> Tx [] and Rx [] </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Timestamp type</td>
 *       <td> SAMPLE_TICKS or REAL_SECONDS or UNIX_EPOCH</td>
 *       <td> SAMPLE_TICKS </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Sample rate (as a hint) </td>
 *       <td> Hz </td>
 *       <td> 0 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Callback </td>
 *       <td> - </td>
 *       <td> nullptr </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> User data </td>
 *       <td> - </td>
 *       <td> nullptr </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Poll </td>
 *       <td> true or false </td>
 *       <td> true </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Sample start on PPS </td>
 *       <td> true or false </td>
 *       <td> false </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Phase alignment </td>
 *       <td> true or false </td>
 *       <td> false </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> Q signal negation </td>
 *       <td> true or false </td>
 *       <td> false </td>
 *    </tr>
 * </table>
 * 
 * <b>Packet size</b> parameter sets the number of samples in a single packet. Internally, the packet size is calculated using bytes. The equation for converting packet size from bytes to samples is given 
 * below the paragraph. Customization of packet size depends on the current device gateware. If the device gateware does not support variable packet sizes, the default packet size will always be <b>4096</b> 
 * bytes. If device gateware supports variable packet sizes, then setting the <b>Packet size</b> parameter to value <b>0</b> will auto set the optimal packet size. Custom packet size can not be larger than 
 * <b>4096</b> bytes. If a larger packet size is specified, the packet size will be clamped to the maximum packet size value on stream setup. Packet must also be a multiple of data bus width. Therefore, 
 * initially specified packet size might be adjusted internally to fit the width of the data bus and can result in a lower packet size then initially anticipated. The final number of samples in a single 
 * packet also depends on the selected size of a single sample (link format parameter) and the number of streaming channels used (channel parameter).
 * 
 * <b> SamplesInPacket = (BytesInPacket - HeaderSize) / (SizeOfSample * ChCount) </b>  
 * 
 * The header size is equal to 16 bytes.
 * 
 * A Table for reference of all possible maximum packet sizes in samples with different channel and sample size parameters:
 * <table>
 *    <tr>
 *       <th> Packet size, samples </th>
 *       <th> Channel count </th>
 *       <th> Single sample size, bytes </th>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 1020 </td>
 *       <td> 1 </td>
 *       <td> 4 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 510 </td>
 *       <td> 2 </td>
 *       <td> 4 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 1360 </td>
 *       <td> 1 </td>
 *       <td> 3 </td>
 *    </tr>
 *    <tr>
 *       <td> 680 </td>
 *       <td> 2 </td>
 *       <td> 3 </td>
 *    </tr>
 * </table>
 * 
 * 
 */